---
// The one place the design system's three families are loaded from. Rendered
// in two heads: the standalone homepage's own <head> (src/pages/[locale]/
// index.astro) and the Starlight shell's, via src/components/Head.astro.
// Declaring `--font-*` in @cypher/ui only *names* the families; without this
// nothing downloads them and the browser silently falls back to system-ui.
//
// The families, weights and styles are configured in astro.config.mjs
// (`fonts`): Astro downloads them at build time and serves them from this
// site. Each <Font /> writes the @font-face rules plus its CSS variable, with
// a metrics-adjusted fallback so text doesn't jump when the real font lands.
//
// Preload only what's on screen at first paint — body text (Inter) and
// headings (Space Grotesk). Preloading every file would compete with the page
// itself for bandwidth.
//
// Filtered by style, not weight: Google serves each family as one variable
// file shared by every weight, and Astro tags that file's preload with only
// the first weight it meets (Space Grotesk: 500), so `{ weight: 600 }` would
// match nothing. `style: 'normal'` is exactly that one non-italic file.
import { Font } from 'astro:assets';
---

<Font cssVariable="--font-inter" preload={[{ style: 'normal' }]} />
<Font cssVariable="--font-space-grotesk" preload={[{ style: 'normal' }]} />
<Font cssVariable="--font-ibm-plex-mono" />
